 All on-chain calls in this version are read-only. The mock tests demonstrate code behavior only and **do not establish real-world safety or independent security-audit certification**.
 
+When returning a block header, native balance, ERC-20 balance/allowance or contract code, `ThreeCoreWalletSession` now checks `eth_chainId` and `eth_accounts` **again after the RPC completes**. Silent chain/account changes during a pending read therefore invalidate the session and discard its output, even if no EIP-1193 event fired. The extra checks use the bounded read deadline and do not request signatures, approval, transfers or automatic reconnection. Run `node --test test/postread-identity-guards.test.js` for offline regression coverage. These mock checks do not establish production wallet compatibility or third-party dApp login.
